## UT-004: Assertion Best Practices

**Scope**: All assertions in test methods

**Assertion Requirements**:
- Every test method must include at least one assertion
- Always provide meaningful assert messages using string variables
- Use appropriate assertion methods based on data type
- Group related assertions logically
- Both `System.assert*()` and `Assert.*()` classes are acceptable

**Assertion Patterns**:

| Assertion Type | System Class Method | Assert Class Method | Example |
|----------------|---------------------|---------------------|---------|
| Equality | `System.assertEquals()` | `Assert.areEqual()` | `Assert.areEqual(expectedCount, actualCount, errorMessage)` |
| Boolean True | `System.assert()` | `Assert.isTrue()` | `Assert.isTrue(result.isSuccess(), successMessage)` |
| Boolean False | `System.assert(!condition)` | `Assert.isFalse()` | `Assert.isFalse(result.hasErrors(), errorMessage)` |
| Null Check | `System.assertNotEquals(null, obj)` | `Assert.isNotNull()` | `Assert.isNotNull(result, nullCheckMessage)` |
| Not Null Check | `System.assertEquals(null, obj)` | `Assert.isNull()` | `Assert.isNull(errorResult, shouldBeNullMessage)` |
| Inequality | `System.assertNotEquals()` | `Assert.areNotEqual()` | `Assert.areNotEqual(oldValue, newValue, changedMessage)` |
| Exception | `try/catch` block | `try/catch` block | Validate expected exceptions are thrown |

**Message Variables**:
```apex
✅ Good Assertion Messages (System class):
String expectedCountMessage = 'Expected 5 accounts, but got different count';
String successMessage = 'Account creation should succeed with valid data';
String nullCheckMessage = 'Result should not be null after successful operation';

System.assertEquals(5, accounts.size(), expectedCountMessage);
System.assert(result.isSuccess(), successMessage);
System.assertNotEquals(null, result, nullCheckMessage);

✅ Good Assertion Messages (Assert class):
String expectedCountMessage = 'Expected 5 accounts, but got different count';
String successMessage = 'Account creation should succeed with valid data';
String nullCheckMessage = 'Result should not be null after successful operation';

Assert.areEqual(5, accounts.size(), expectedCountMessage);
Assert.isTrue(result.isSuccess(), successMessage);
Assert.isNotNull(result, nullCheckMessage);

❌ Bad Assertions:
System.assertEquals(5, accounts.size());           // No message
System.assert(result.isSuccess(), 'failed');       // Vague message
Assert.areEqual(5, accounts.size());               // No message
Assert.isTrue(result.isSuccess(), 'failed');       // Vague message
```

